.MARINE...
(Today through Tuesday)
Issued at 1101 AM PDT Thu Sep 3 2026

Rain chances increase over the northern waters through the day as
a weak cold front moves through the region. Southwesterly winds
gradually shift northwesterly by this afternoon after cold frontal
passage. Winds generally stay gentle to moderate but diurnal
fresh to strong gusts return within the Monterey Bay and along the
Big Sur Coast Friday into the weekend. More widespread fresh to
strong gusts return by early next week across the coastal waters.
Long period southerly swell associated with tropical activity well
to our south will reach the coastal waters Friday and continue
into early next week.

